From 757b6211900f210e11d4a000cae6b56ac0a63efc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Roch=C3=A9=20Compaan?= <roche@upfrontsoftware.co.za>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:22:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 13/14] qwen35: compare the dense graph against a
 double-precision reference

tests/test_qwen35_oracle.c builds a two-layer dense qwen35 in one host buffer
(F32 tensors, head_dim 256, n_head 2, n_head_kv 1, n_embd 512, vocab 32) and runs
qwen4_graph_forward_tokens for one token at position 0. The reference implements
the documented layer order in double precision: embedding row, per-layer
rmsnorm, the mixer (recurrent delta rule or gated attention), the residual add,
the FFN's rmsnorm and swiglu, the second residual add, and the final norm with
the output head.

Three cases: interval 1 (both layers attention, so a failure cannot hide behind
the recurrent mixer), and interval 2 once through the fused decode front and
once through DS4_QWEN4_NO_FUSE's plain ops. Measured max |device - reference|:
3.2e-06, 3.6e-05 and 3.6e-05 against the 1e-3 bar; repeats are bit identical.

One token at position 0 keeps the attention contract small: a single cached key
makes the softmax 1, so a head's output is its value rounded to the half cache
times sigmoid(gate). Rope and the q/k norms are covered by Task 4's suite. The
reference omits the alpha projection because the decay multiplies a zero state.

Two fault injections prove the comparison discriminates: sigmoid for silu in
qwen35_cuda::gdn_out fails at 1.40 while the attention-only case stays at
3.2e-06, and an FFN normalisation reading attn_norm fails at 0.24. Both were
reverted. An earlier version of this test passed the first injection because
every tensor was scaled at 1/sqrt(width), which put the logits near 1e-2; gamma
vectors now centre on 1.

A fourth case compares nine tokens in one forward against the same nine decoded
one at a time, which is where a batch-only dispatch or state fault shows up
without any weights: measured max |batch - serial| = 1.5e-05, and reading the
row before the last trips it at 1.6 while the reference cases stay green.
Named test-qwen35-oracle, not test-qwen35-graph: that target already exists and
drives tests/test_qwen4_kernels with DS4_TEST_QWEN35_GRAPH_ONLY=1 on Metal.

The serial side is nine one-token forwards, so every recurrent state transition
is the serial one, not an eight-token prefix followed by one step.

Upstream: not offered, fork only
Retire-when: dense qwen35 runs on CUDA upstream
Carried-commits: none (authored here)
